    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172-a8">

                <pb facs="0385" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg285"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No. 705.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carson to Mr.
                            Bandinel.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Bandinel</hi>: In reply to your letter of
                    the 18th instant, I beg to state that the secular subjects taught in the school
                    are geography, penmanship, and the course of reading-books taught in the
                    government school at Hong-Kong.</p>
                <p>These reading-books, four in number, in a graduated series, treat of a great
                    variety of subjects, both foreign and native. As soon as the children are far
                    enough advanced they will be taught arithmetic and other subjects.</p>
                <p>The school is a free boarding-school supported by the mission, and our object is
                    to train for ourselves a staff of native helpers.</p>
                <p>Believe me, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES CARSON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
